@titaiwangms Addressed the registry merge risk in ffa30bfbc by syncing with current main. Both schema declarations and `ForEachSchema` preserve Gemm-29, GroupedMatMul-29, and LogCumSumExp-29. The rebuilt library exposes all 631 upstream standard-domain schema/version registrations, and regenerated documentation includes all three opset-29 schemas. LogCumSumExp's specification and semantics are unchanged.

The operator, schema, and inliner tests pass, including repeated LogCumSumExp expansion with overlapping intermediate names, strict shape inference, full checking, and execution. The narrow GPT-5.6 Sol review found no merge regression.

For the shared-inliner question, #8693 is not merged into this base. A separate probe reproduced the existing root-only type-lookup limitation when chained context-dependent functions consume branch-local values inside `If`, with both LogCumSumExp and existing Softmax. This is not a name-collision finding or a regression introduced here; nested branch-local lookup remains a shared-inliner follow-up.
